    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: CE-4692 BL-S2 (docs/designs/engineering/DESIGN_Bridge_Laying.md §5) — on basic-desert a RIVER (an authored Water feature, y 60-72 across the whole map) is spanned by a scenario-placed LAID BRIDGE (an assault span, TKB 8825, 600 hp) at (80, 66), heading north. 'Tank On Bridge' (an M1) drives onto the deck and parks at its centre. 'Charge Man' waits 35 s on the far bank, walks onto the deck near its north end (80, 73) and sets off his 8 kg demolition charge: the blast is measured to the DECK (not the entity's centre) and drops the span; every man or vehicle on the span as it falls goes into the river — the tank is destroyed (there is no water model: nothing swims, Q-3); the deck is no floor at once, the navmesh and the road follow at the rebake; a fallen laid bridge leaves NO rubble. 'Second Tank' waits at (60, 20) for 70 s, then is ordered to (60, 110) on the far bank: with the bridge gone there is no way across. Judge: the charge bursts; the objective 'blow the bridge' ends Achieved; the objective 'the tank on the bridge is lost' ends Achieved; the second tank never stands north of the river. Fail: the bridge survives, the tank on it survives, or the second tank crosses. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh bl-blow-the-bridge"
  },
